{"ts":"2026-07-13T09:32:01.899Z","author":"maintainer-agent","op":"create","patch":[{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/id","value":"pm-9k90"},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/title","value":"MCP tool profiles: core/standard/full/custom tiers with an allowlist override, so 28 tools are the maximum surface, not the default"},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/description","value":"Tier the MCP tool surface: core (~10 tools: pm_next, pm_context, pm_search, pm_get, pm_create, pm_claim, pm_update, pm_close, pm_plan, pm_validate), standard (adds workflow+evidence: pm_append, pm_files, pm_docs, pm_notes, pm_learnings, pm_deps, pm_test, pm_health, pm_profile, pm_config), full (all narrow tools + pm_run), custom (env/config allowlist e.g. PM_MCP_TOOLS=pm_next,pm_context,...). pm_run stays a fallback for advanced/low-frequency operations, never the first tool an agent sees. Distinct new feature — does NOT reopen the dispositioned pm-mpbb DX lever list (a-d)."},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/type","value":"Feature"},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/status","value":"open"},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/priority","value":2},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/tags","value":["agents","ergonomics","mcp","token-surface"]},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/created_at","value":"2026-07-13T09:32:01.899Z"},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/updated_at","value":"2026-07-13T09:32:01.899Z"},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/author","value":"maintainer-agent"},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/estimated_minutes","value":480},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/acceptance_criteria","value":"Profile selection via MCP server config/env with core as a deliberate product decision for the default; tools/list payload for core measured via scripts/measure-agent-token-surface.mjs and published (baseline: 28 tools = 32979 B ~= 8.2k tokens per pm-a22j); custom allowlist validated against known tool names with clear errors; profiles documented in registry metadata and plugin docs; contract/drift gates cover per-profile tool sets; existing integration suites pass under every profile"},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/parent","value":"pm-mpbb"},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/risk","value":"low"},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/confidence","value":"high"},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/dependencies","value":[{"id":"pm-wjfa","kind":"related","created_at":"2026-07-13T09:32:01.899Z"}]}],"before_hash":"3cc22dff72be7b14824654a7a64ea62b04799939b2fee54c1b5f52ca60bf6df0","after_hash":"26d8656e88c90319785a94407ac7c76cb0f25a8eeef62d4f1afb7113828ec5d0","message":""}
{"ts":"2026-07-13T09:32:19.589Z","author":"maintainer-agent","op":"note_add","patch":[{"op":"replace","path":"/metadata/updated_at","value":"2026-07-13T09:32:19.589Z"},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/notes","value":[{"created_at":"2026-07-13T09:32:19.589Z","author":"maintainer-agent","text":"Rationale evidence: June 2026 tool-selection study (arxiv 2606.30317) found substantial accuracy degradation as available tool count grows (threshold varies by model); Task Master independently ships core/standard/full MCP tiers with explicit token budgets for the same reason. Pair with MCP resources+prompts (owned by pm-z3ez) so stable reference context does not need to be a tool. Selection quality is an agent-acquisition lever, not just a token saving — a smaller, sharper surface makes agents pick pm tools correctly more often."}]}],"before_hash":"26d8656e88c90319785a94407ac7c76cb0f25a8eeef62d4f1afb7113828ec5d0","after_hash":"d5ac3e77946a3d6ff2b9c80c679eb29de1021387ddda7fb5c5414dd48aa06abf"}
{"ts":"2026-07-15T19:27:28.270Z","author":"maintainer-agent","op":"note_add","patch":[{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/notes/1","value":{"created_at":"2026-07-15T19:27:28.263Z","author":"maintainer-agent","text":"Re-measurement 2026-07-15 (review pass #89, scripts/measure-agent-token-surface.mjs): MCP tools/list 33,314 B / 8,329 tokens / 28 tools — up from the pm-a22j baseline 32,979 B (2026-07-11). Every session with the MCP server attached pays ~8.3k tokens before the first call, and each new tool/flag grows it; the core/standard/full profile tiers this item owns are the structural fix. Companion figure: full-format single-item surface is 539,946 B (~135k tokens) vs summary_json 4,426 B — the 122x spread shows how much the profile/format choices matter for agent context budgets."}},{"op":"replace","path":"/metadata/updated_at","value":"2026-07-15T19:27:28.270Z"}],"before_hash":"d5ac3e77946a3d6ff2b9c80c679eb29de1021387ddda7fb5c5414dd48aa06abf","after_hash":"6ef3cfd3436eedac6e3ce11c947fb4a5c45d04e0564c20b2e934deae12f2bf25"}
